const e=JSON.parse(`[{"id":"PC_E5_001","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Anybody setting up a new business or factory has to comply with a plethora of statutory requirements. It is not argued here that regulations are bad. But the rules should not be so unrealistically stringent as to make compliance impossible. It appears that the purpose of regulation is not to enforce responsible behaviour among people and protect society but to provide an avenue for corrupt officials to make easy money.","options":{"A":"It seems that our laws serve as a fertile breeding ground for corruption.","B":"It seems that strict laws are made not to be observed but to be paid lip service with the connivance of corrupt officials.","C":"It seems that Indian laws are typically known for their complexity, obtuseness and ambiguity.","D":"It seems that the statute book is littered with obsolete laws which have outlived their utility."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"It seems that strict laws are made not to be observed but to be paid lip service with the connivance of corrupt officials.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Implies the laws themselves are the source of corruption, whereas the paragraph argues it is the difficulty in compliance — not the laws per se — that creates the avenue for corruption.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"Brings out the idea that strict laws create a situation where compliance is bypassed with the connivance of corrupt officials — in tune with the tone and spirit of the paragraph."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Nowhere in the preceding sentences is it implied that the laws are complex, obtuse or ambiguous — this is outside the scope of the paragraph.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"The paragraph does not imply that the laws are obsolete or outdated — this introduces a concept not discussed.","error_type":"out_of_scope"}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","C":"out_of_scope","D":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The paragraph talks about the stringent nature of Indian laws, too stringent to make compliance almost impossible. It also mentions that this results in an avenue for the corrupt officials. Any sentence that is to complete the paragraph should continue with this idea.\\nOption A: incorrect because it implies that the very laws are the source for corruption, while it is the difficulty in compliance that results in corruption.\\nOption B: correct it brings out an idea that is in tune with the tone and spirit of the paragraph.\\nOption C: incorrect because nowhere in the preceding sentences is it implied that the laws are complex.\\nOption D: incorrect because the paragraph does not imply that the laws of obsolete (outdated).\\nThus, the best option is Option B. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_002","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Animals living near colder climates are bigger in size because being heftier allows them several benefits like reducing body heat loss, according to researchers. For most species of vertebrates, body mass increases the closer you get to the poles. The bigger you are, the more fat you can store to help you get through the winter.","options":{"A":"So, there are several factors that can affect an animal's body size and weight.","B":"So, this is how animals deal with issues of heat loss and heat regulation in the cold.","C":"So, a big body helps reduce heat loss.","D":"So, it pays to be bigger in the colder climates that exist at high latitudes and altitudes."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"So, it pays to be bigger in the colder climates that exist at high latitudes and altitudes.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about several factors while temperature and cold climate is the only factor given in the paragraph — introduces a breadth not supported.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Heat regulation is not the central point of discussion — the paragraph focuses specifically on heat loss, not the broader concept of heat regulation.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not contain the significant factor of colder climate mentioned throughout the paragraph — too narrow a conclusion.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Aptly captures the essence of the paragraph to arrive at a generalisation that can be properly drawn from the information given — combines body size with the cold climate context."}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","B":"wrong_focus","C":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The paragraph talks about the significance of body size in surviving in colder climates. It posits that the higher the body size, the better the prevention of heat loss in cold climate. This sense is substantiated by pointing at the bigger body size of animals at the poles. A sentence that aptly completes this paragraph should continue in this vein.\\nOption A: incorrect because this sentence talks about several factors while temperature is the only factor given in the paragraph.\\nOption B: incorrect because this talks about heat regulation which is not the central point of discussion in the paragraph.\\nOption C: incorrect because this sentence does not contain the significant factor – colder climate – mentioned in the paragraph.\\nOption D: correct because it aptly captures the essence to arrive at a generalization that can be properly drawn from the information given in the paragraph.\\nThus, the best option is Option D. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_003","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"A beetle species - the size of a grain of rice - has increased the summer temperatures in Canada's British Columbia by one degree Celsius after wiping out huge forest area, researchers claim. Scientists say by reducing the amount of water pumped into the air by vegetation, the beetle has had as big an impact on local climate as forest fires.","options":{"A":"The increase in temperature has resulted from the Sun's energy heating up the ground surface instead of being used up for evaporating water.","B":"The increase in temperature has resulted from cloud formation due to evaporation of water.","C":"The increase in temperature has resulted from the altering of rain fall pattern.","D":"It is an established fact that beetle attacks always cause climate change."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"The increase in temperature has resulted from the Sun's energy heating up the ground surface instead of being used up for evaporating water.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"Correctly explains how heat not used in the evaporation process (because vegetation is reduced) raises the temperature — adds the proper scientific explanation needed in context."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Logically illogical — with cloud formation, temperature decreases, not increases as stated in the paragraph.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The relation between temperature increase and rainfall pattern cannot be established from the information given — outside the scope.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"We cannot decisively declare the causal relation between beetle species and temperature rise as an established fact based on the information given — too extreme and overgeneralises.","error_type":"too_extreme"}},"common_errors":{"B":"contradicts_paragraph","C":"out_of_scope","D":"too_extreme"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The passage describes the role of a beetle species, which has increased the temperature by resulting in the forest loss. The concluding sentence should perhaps bring out the cause for this temperature increase.\\nOption A: correct because this explains how heat not used in evaporation process raises the temperature. This adds a proper explanation needed in the context.\\nOption B: incorrect because this sentence is illogical; with the cloud formation, temperature decreases; it does not increase as stated in the paragraph.\\nOption C: incorrect because the relation between temperature increase and rainfall pattern cannot be talked about because it is outside the scope of information given.\\nOption D: incorrect because we cannot decisively declare the causal relation between the beetle species and temperature raise, basing on the information given.\\nThus, the best option is Option A. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_004","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Water tables, laid down over thousands (if not millions) of years, are fast disappearing. Mountain glaciers, the source of many rivers and storehouses of fresh water, are receding within the lifetime of a sherpa. Traditional fisheries are disappearing so fast that fishermen have to venture farther and farther out for ever-smaller catches. Many staple fish species have become extinct in their catchment areas. Our existing method of agriculture is able to feed an ever-growing population because of its unsustainable use of petrochemical-based fertilizers.","options":{"A":"Once petrol supplies disappear, mass extinction will be upon us.","B":"Once petrol supplies disappear, we are certain to face mass starvation.","C":"The disappearance of petrol supplies will spell doom for us.","D":"Once petrol supplies disappear, vehicles will be run on solar energy."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Once petrol supplies disappear, we are certain to face mass starvation.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Mass extinction is too far-fetched a conclusion — the paragraph is about food supply and starvation, not species extinction.","error_type":"too_extreme"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"Gives a logical continuation by mentioning mass starvation — an imminent danger of running out of petrol supplies given agriculture's dependence on petrochemical-based fertilizers."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The use of 'doom' makes this option far-fetched and vague — not specific enough to the food supply context.","error_type":"vague"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Sustenance and food supply is the point of interest, not the use of vehicles — completely outside the scope of the paragraph.","error_type":"out_of_scope"}},"common_errors":{"A":"too_extreme","C":"vague","D":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The paragraph talks about the disappearance of the water table, and its effects on food availability for humans. The penultimate sentence states that our existing agriculture, which depends on petrochemical-based fertilizers, is now able to feed human population. The sentence to continue the paragraph needs to tell either the potential danger or another possible effect of the disappearance of the water table.\\nOption A: incorrect because the concept of mass extinction mentioned in this option is rather too far-fetched.\\nOption B: correct because it goes on to give a logical continuation by mentioning mass starvation, an imminent danger of running out of petrol supplies, given agriculture's dependence on petrochemical-based fertilizers.\\nOption C: incorrect because the use of the word doom makes this option far-fetched.\\nOption D: incorrect because the sustenance, not the use of vehicles, is the point of interest.\\nThus, the best option is Option B. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_005","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Sir John's school experience suggests another truth: views and predictions by 'experts' should never be treated as if they were sacrosanct. Experts can be wrong. He is not of course suggesting that experts should automatically be disbelieved. That would be ridiculous. Their expertise is important, and it should clearly always be taken seriously.","options":{"A":"The point that he is making is that it is not important to consider experts' views.","B":"The point that he is making is that it is important just to examine things critically.","C":"The point that he is making is that in considering what experts say, it is important not to close one's mind.","D":"The point is that that one should be sceptical of everything."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"The point that he is making is that in considering what experts say, it is important not to close one's mind.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"The paragraph explicitly states that experts' views are important and should be taken seriously — this option directly contradicts that.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not contain the important element of experts' opinions — the paragraph specifically talks about how to approach expert views, not just general critical examination.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":true,"reason":"Brings out the correct view — experts should be taken seriously but one should not close one's mind to the possibility that they can be wrong."},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"The use of 'everything' makes this too extreme — the paragraph is specifically about expert opinion, not universal scepticism.","error_type":"too_extreme"}},"common_errors":{"A":"contradicts_paragraph","B":"wrong_focus","D":"too_extreme"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The paragraph talks about Sir John's view on experts' opinion. He posits that their views are not 'sacrosanct' and so we must view them with a healthy skepticism. Thus, the sentence that completes the paragraph should bring out this view.\\nOption A: incorrect because it is important to consider experts' views because the paragraph posits that their expertise is important.\\nOption B: incorrect because this option does not contain the important element mentioned in the passage (experts' opinion).\\nOption C: correct because it brings out the view required by the context.\\nOption D: incorrect because of the use of everything.\\nThus, the best option is Option C. Choice (C)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_006","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Every year, one typical coal-fired power station devours several million tonnes of fuel and produces even more carbon dioxide. Burning stuff has the virtue that it is simple but it is very brutal. The volume of carbon dioxide is damaging the atmosphere and, in the longer term, the fuel will run out.","options":{"A":"If we want to get energy without burning fossil fuels then there is a huge gap to fill.","B":"Renewable energy sources can't satisfy the demand.","C":"Fusion is always the fuel of the future.","D":"It is clear that the world needs an alternative to generating energy by setting fire to things."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"It is clear that the world needs an alternative to generating energy by setting fire to things.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"The gap between power production and power demand is not the point of interest in the paragraph — the paragraph focuses on the problems with burning fuel, not on a supply gap.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"The inability of renewable sources to satisfy power needs is not the focus — this introduces a different debate not supported by the paragraph.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The adequacy of fusion is completely outside the scope of the information given.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Completes the paragraph logically within the limits of information given — the need for an alternative to burning things follows directly from the two problems stated: atmospheric damage and fuel depletion."}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"out_of_scope","C":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The main idea of the paragraph is that coal-fired power stations are not only depleting resources but also polluting the environment by adding gases such as carbon dioxide. The sentence that completes the paragraph should be in tune with this information.\\nOption A: incorrect the gap between power production and power demand is not the point of interest in the paragraph.\\nOption B: incorrect because the inability of renewable sources to satisfy the power needs is not the focus of the paragraph.\\nOption C: incorrect because the adequacy of fusion is outside the scope of the paragraph.\\nOption D: correct because it completes the paragraph logically within the limits of information given.\\nThus, the best option is Option D. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_007","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Courage allows you to run your own race. Courage allows you to do whatever you want to do because you know that it is right. Courage gives you the self-control to persist where others have failed.","options":{"A":"Ultimately, courage is a quality that everyone could cultivate.","B":"Ultimately, courage pays huge dividends over the long run.","C":"Ultimately, abundance of courage is absolutely necessary in life.","D":"Ultimately, the degree of courage you live with determines the amount of fulfillment you receive."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Ultimately, the degree of courage you live with determines the amount of fulfillment you receive.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"We cannot infer from the paragraph that everyone could cultivate courage — the paragraph describes what courage does, not whether it can be cultivated by all.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Two expressions — 'huge dividends' and 'long run' — are not justified by the information given; neither financial returns nor time horizon are mentioned.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The categorical term 'absolutely' makes this too extreme — the information given does not support such a categorical statement.","error_type":"too_extreme"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"The phrases 'run the race' and 'persist where others have failed' in the paragraph justify this option — the degree of courage determines fulfilment received."}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","B":"out_of_scope","C":"too_extreme"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The paragraph talks about the virtue of courage and about how it helps us. Given the too-generic sense, it might be tricky or difficult to guess what is needed to complete the passage. For such a question, process of elimination is the best strategy.\\nOption A: incorrect because we cannot infer that everyone could cultivate the virtue of courage.\\nOption B: incorrect because two expressions (huge dividends and long run) make this option questionable and beyond the scope of the information given.\\nOption C: incorrect because of the categorical term absolutely. The information given does not support this categorical statement.\\nOption D: correct because the phrases run the race and persist where others have failed justify this option as the correct sentence.\\nThus, the correct option is Option D. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_008","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"As a physician who has been deeply privileged to share the most profound moments of people's lives, including their final moments, let me tell you a secret. People facing death don't think about what degrees they have earned, what positions they have held or how much wealth they have accumulated. At the end, what really matters is who you loved and who loved you.","options":{"A":"Love is composed of a single soul inhabiting two bodies.","B":"Being deeply loved by someone gives you strength, while loving someone deeply gives you courage.","C":"The circle of love is everything.","D":"Sometimes the heart sees what is invisible to the eye."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"The circle of love is everything.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"The mention of 'soul' is out of context — the paragraph focuses on the practical reality of love at end of life, not philosophical definitions of love.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"The use of 'courage' and 'strength' is not justified — these concepts are not mentioned or implied in the paragraph which focuses solely on love.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":true,"reason":"Emphasises love as the ultimate measure of life — in tune with the paragraph's central point that what matters at the end is love."},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"The concept of invisible things being seen by the heart is irrelevant to the context of the paragraph.","error_type":"out_of_scope"}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","B":"out_of_scope","D":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The paragraph posits that at the time of death, what matters is the love you receive or you offer. Overall, the paragraph implies that love is important at the end of the day. The correct option should reflect this.\\nOption A: incorrect because this information is out of context because of the mention of soul.\\nOption B: incorrect because the use of the words courage and strength is not justified.\\nOption C: correct because this emphasizes love.\\nOption D: incorrect because this concept is irrelevant to the context.\\nThus, the best option is Option C. Choice (C)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_009","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Pessimism is a very easy way out because it is a short view of life. If you look at what is happening around us today, you can't help but feel that life is a terrible complexity of problems. But if you look back a few thousand years, you realize that we have advanced fantastically.","options":{"A":"If you take a long view, I do not see how you can be pessimistic about the future of mankind.","B":"Nevertheless, it would be wrong to be too pessimistic.","C":"At my age it is unseemly to be pessimistic.","D":"I get pessimistic sometimes but not for long."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"If you take a long view, I do not see how you can be pessimistic about the future of mankind.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"Correctly captures the idea implied by the paragraph — in the long run, the human race has advanced despite short-term hiccups, so pessimism is unjustified when a long view is taken."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"The expression 'too pessimistic' implies some pessimism is acceptable — but the paragraph argues against pessimism as a whole, not just excess pessimism.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The reference to 'my age' is not justified — there is no first-person age context in the paragraph.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"The temporary nature of pessimism is not what the paragraph argues — it argues that a long view makes pessimism untenable.","error_type":"wrong_focus"}},"common_errors":{"B":"wrong_focus","C":"out_of_scope","D":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The paragraph talks about pessimism with rejection because of its myopic view. If we look at the phrases used, we can understand that in the long run, human race advanced despite short-term hiccups. Any sentence that completes the paragraph should reflect this tone and idea.\\nOption A: correct because this is the idea implied as per the above explanation.\\nOption B: incorrect because of the expression too pessimistic.\\nOption C: incorrect because the reference to the age is not justified in this option.\\nOption D: incorrect because the temporary nature of pessimism is not justified.\\nThus, the best option is Option A. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_010","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"It is a good idea to be ambitious, to have goals, to want to be good at what you do, but it is a terrible mistake to let drive and ambition get in the way of treating people with kindness and decency. The point is not that they will then be nice to you.","options":{"A":"It is that you will feel better about yourself.","B":"It is that if you are nice to people on your way up, you'll meet them on your way down.","C":"It is that you just suck up and be nice.","D":"It is that you should be nice to each other, and don't step on other people's toes and infringe on their freedom."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"It is that you will feel better about yourself.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"The last sentence posits that the point is NOT that others will be nice to you — so the point must be something personal and intrinsic. Feeling better about yourself is the implied personal benefit of treating others with kindness."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Their treatment towards us is exactly what the paragraph says is NOT the point — this option directly contradicts the last sentence.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Not relevant to the context — the paragraph is about genuine kindness, not about sycophancy.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Ignores the important piece of information in the last sentence that the point is NOT about others being nice to you — this option is too generic.","error_type":"vague"}},"common_errors":{"B":"contradicts_paragraph","C":"out_of_scope","D":"vague"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The paragraph suggests that being kind and decent to others is important even though we have ambitious plans or goals. The last sentence posits that the point is not that they will be nice to you. This implies that the kindness and decency would give us satisfaction on personal grounds. The sentence that completes the paragraph should give this sense.\\nOption A: correct because this gives the sense explained above.\\nOption B: incorrect because their treatment towards us is not the point of interest in the paragraph.\\nOption C: incorrect because this is not relevant to the context.\\nOption D: incorrect because this ignores the important piece of information present in the last sentence.\\nThus, the correct option is Option A. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_011","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Everyone on this planet is a wonder of this world. Every one of us is a hero in some way or another. Every one of us has a potential for extraordinary achievement, happiness and lasting fulfillment.","options":{"A":"Positive habits will create results.","B":"Do what you truly love to do.","C":"Small victories will lead to large victories.","D":"All it takes are small steps in the direction of our dreams."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"All it takes are small steps in the direction of our dreams.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"The passage does not imply positive habits — it focuses on individual potential and the possibility of extraordinary achievement.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Whether doing what we love results in great achievements is not mentioned in the paragraph — the paragraph focuses on potential, not on what action to take.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Ignores the component of individual potential — the paragraph is about each person's inherent potential, not about strategy.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Reflects the idea that everyone's extraordinary potential can be realised through small steps — consistent with the paragraph's message about universal potential."}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","B":"out_of_scope","C":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The paragraph talks about individual potential; all of us have a potential to achieve extraordinary things. The sentence that completes the paragraph should reflect this potential.\\nOption A: incorrect because the passage does not imply positive habits.\\nOption B: incorrect because whether or not doing what we love results in great achievements is not mentioned in the paragraph.\\nOption C: incorrect because this ignores the component of individual potential.\\nOption D: correct because this reflects the idea mentioned in the above explanation.\\nThus, the best option is Option D. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_012","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"The one-piece swimsuit by a famous luxury brand that sold out last week despite warnings that it should not be worn in pools is but the most recent example of how shallow fashion has become these days. According to the label, the material used for the sleek, retro item reacts adversely to chlorine, commonly found in swimming pools. Clearly, neither that little drawback nor the fact that it costs nearly $400, deterred fashionistas from snapping it up, to wear as a crease-free top – called bodysuits back in the day - with skirts and trousers, as the promotional tag advised.","options":{"A":"And this new genre of incongruous clothing is only increasing.","B":"For many garments and accessories targeted at the youth, being Insta-compatible appears to be the main intention.","C":"We need a new classification – futile fashion.","D":"It appears that compatibility with pools need not be an essential attribute of swimwear."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"It appears that compatibility with pools need not be an essential attribute of swimwear.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"'New genre' suggests there are other items like this, but the paragraph refers only to this specific swimsuit — no other items are mentioned.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"No other garments and accessories are mentioned in the paragraph — the option goes beyond the scope of the single example discussed.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Too general and vague — makes no reference to the swimsuit specifically discussed in the paragraph.","error_type":"vague"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Highlights the most striking aspect of the specific swimsuit becoming fashionable despite being incompatible with pools — directly concludes the single example discussed."}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","B":"out_of_scope","C":"vague"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"A comment that can conclude the paragraph that cites an example of a swimsuit incompatible with pools becoming popular is option D; it highlights the most striking aspect of this swimsuit becoming fashionable.\\nOption A: 'New genre' suggests there are other items too, but the paragraph refers to no such items, making choice A inappropriate.\\nOption B: This option can be eliminated on the same grounds since no other garments and accessories are mentioned in the paragraph.\\nOption C: This option is too general and vague to go with the paragraph; it makes no reference to the swimsuit.\\nOption D: correct based on the explanation given at the beginning Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_013","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"The term deconstruction was derived from the French Philosopher Jacques Derrida's 1967 work, 'Of Grammatology'. Deconstruction is a form of semiotic analysis. Derrida was of the opinion that all texts should be deconstructed and that binary oppositions should be used to assign meaning and values. According to him, the first task in deconstruction would be that of overturning binary opposition. To fully comprehend this, a reader must understand that in a text, he/she is dealing with violent hierarchy as opposed to peaceful coexistence. For example, signified over signifier, activity over passivity, man over woman etc.","options":{"A":"The process of overturning, is of trivial importance when it comes to deconstruction.","B":"Binary oppositions exist in texts, and according to Derrida, they should be constructed.","C":"In other words, as a result of the violent hierarchy, one word of each pair is a victim of oppression.","D":"Deconstruction would involve overturning the hierarchy at a given moment."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Deconstruction would involve overturning the hierarchy at a given moment.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"The word 'trivial' directly undermines the emphasis Derrida attributed to overturning — contradicts the paragraph's central argument.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"The paragraph states binary oppositions should be overturned, not constructed — this is a direct contradiction.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The concept of oppression is not mentioned or implied in the paragraph — introduces a new concept not discussed.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Reflects the idea in tune with the ideas presented — deconstruction involves overturning the hierarchy, which is exactly what Derrida's first task was."}},"common_errors":{"A":"contradicts_paragraph","B":"contradicts_paragraph","C":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The main idea of the paragraph is Derrida's theory of deconstruction. In his opinion, deconstruction, a form of semiotic analysis, involves overturning binary opposition. The reader of a text should deal with violent hierarchy as opposed to peaceful coexistence. The sentence that completes the paragraph should be in tune with this idea or reflect this idea.\\nOption A: this is wrong because of the word trivial, which undermines the emphasis Derrida attributed to overturning.\\nOption B: incorrect because the passage does not imply that the binary oppositions should be constructed.\\nOption C: incorrect because the concept of oppression is not mentioned or implied.\\nOption D: correct because this reflects the idea in tune with the ideas presented in the paragraph.\\nThus, the correct option is Option D. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_014","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Mercury is the innermost planet in the solar system. It is the smallest of all planets and the most eccentric. It orbits the sun once in about eighty eight earth days. Mercury's surface is similar to that of the earth's moon and it is heavily cratered indicating that it has been geologically inactive for billions of years. Mercury's axis has the smallest tilt compared to that of any other planet in the solar system.","options":{"A":"However, Mercury's orbital eccentricity is the largest.","B":"A large number of craters is a characteristic of Mercury.","C":"However, Mercury's orbital eccentricity is the smallest.","D":"The tilt of the Earth's axis is more than that of Mercury's."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"However, Mercury's orbital eccentricity is the largest.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"The tilt being smallest and orbital eccentricity being largest are logically connected by 'however' — smallest tilt contrasted with largest eccentricity creates a meaningful contrast about Mercury's extremes."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"The sentence immediately before is about axis tilt, not craters — this option does not follow logically from the preceding sentence.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"'However' should show contrast with the earlier sentence — but both sentences express something smallest (tilt AND eccentricity), making the contrast meaningless.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not gel with the earlier sentence — the paragraph is about Mercury's characteristics, not about comparison with Earth's axis.","error_type":"wrong_focus"}},"common_errors":{"B":"wrong_focus","C":"contradicts_paragraph","D":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The paragraph describes the peculiarities of the planet Mercury. It gives various characteristic features of Mercury. The last sentence talks about the smallest tilt of the planet. The next sentence, which is to conclude the paragraph, should give the continuation of or a contrast with this idea.\\nOption A: correct because the tilt being smallest and orbital eccentricity being largest are logically connected by the conjunctive however, which is present in the option.\\nOption B: incorrect because the sentence immediately before the sentence in this option is not about craters.\\nOption C: incorrect because the use of however in this option should show contrast with the earlier sentence, not similarity; both sentences express something smallest.\\nOption D: incorrect because this sentence does not gel with the earlier sentence.\\nThus, the best option is Option A. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_015","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"International health experts are warning of a mounting health crisis in parts of Africa because of an influx of counterfeit medicine from Asia that is playing havoc with the treatment of diseases such as malaria. Porous borders in Africa, coupled with indifferent oversight in China, are combining to turn the continent and its pressing health problems into a free-for-all for maverick manufacturers, some of whom are producing pills with no active ingredients at all.","options":{"A":"We have recognised this problem.","B":"Efforts to combat the activity are in their infancy.","C":"This causes drug resistance building all over Africa.","D":"This problem has not been addressed so far."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Efforts to combat the activity are in their infancy.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"The use of present perfect tense ('have recognised') is illogical given that the preceding sentence uses present continuous tense — indicating the problem is ongoing and not yet fully recognised.","error_type":"tense_mismatch"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"'Efforts to combat the activity' — 'the activity' refers to the problem of counterfeit medicines. This correctly continues the paragraph by indicating the response is nascent."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Drug resistance is not related to the concept — scientifically, medicines with no active ingredients cannot cause drug resistance.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"'So far' implies the problem has been known to people — but the present continuous tense in the preceding sentence implies the problem is still emerging and being discovered.","error_type":"tense_mismatch"}},"common_errors":{"A":"tense_mismatch","C":"contradicts_paragraph","D":"tense_mismatch"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The paragraph talks about health problems created in Africa because of spurious medicines exported from China. In fact, the paragraph says, there are no active ingredients in medicines supplied. The continuing sentence should expand this thought of counterfeit medicine, a problem that is still present.\\nOption A: incorrect because the use of present continuous in the earlier sentence makes the present perfect tense in this option illogical.\\nOption B: correct because this sentence has the expression efforts to combat the activity, the last word referring to the problem of counterfeit medicines mentioned in the earlier sentence.\\nOption C: incorrect because the concept of drug resistance is not related to the concept; in fact, scientifically speaking, if the medicines consist of no active ingredient at all, they cannot cause drug resistance.\\nOption D: incorrect because the use of so far in this sentence implies that the problem has been known to people, but that is not the case; note the use of the present continuous tense in the earlier sentence.\\nThus, the best option is Option B. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_016","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"Genocide does not appear out of thin air. In most cases there are years, even decades, in which we could detect the warning signs, if we could be bothered. It would be less expensive in lives and money if we reacted when the hate propaganda began, rather than when the mass graves are being unearthed.","options":{"A":"War criminals continue to travel the world relatively freely, without fear of arrest.","B":"Our words of condemnation rarely match our willingness to enforce existing international conventions.","C":"Yet there is no need for new international laws to apprehend alleged war criminals.","D":"Action now is less costly than paying for peacekeeping forces and refugee camps."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Action now is less costly than paying for peacekeeping forces and refugee camps.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about war criminals but not about genocide prevention — outside the scope of the paragraph's argument about early intervention.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not talk about the preventive measures implied in the paragraph — the paragraph argues for early action, not about condemnation vs enforcement.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The spirit of the sentence goes against the suggested prevention of genocide — the paragraph advocates for early action, not for the adequacy of existing laws.","error_type":"tone_mismatch"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Continues the idea of preventive measures hinted at — 'less expensive' echoes 'less expensive in lives and money' in the preceding sentence, completing the cost-benefit argument for early action."}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","B":"wrong_focus","C":"tone_mismatch"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Overall, the paragraph argues that genocide is not a sudden phenomenon, but a phenomenon that gradually results from the budding signs of hatred. The last sentence of the paragraph should continue the idea that it can be better prevented at an earlier stage, rather than at a later stage.\\nOption A: incorrect because this talks about war criminals, but not about genocide.\\nOption B: incorrect because this sentence does not talk about the preventive measures implied in the paragraph.\\nOption C: incorrect because the spirit of the sentence goes against the suggested prevention of genocide.\\nOption D: correct because this option continues the idea of preventive measures hinted at.\\nThus, the best option is Option D. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_017","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"We hear of numerous studies from all over the globe about the increasing number of people with diabetes. The single most important reason in addition to genetic factors seems to be obesity, particularly the abdominal fat. Studies have shown that by adopting a healthy lifestyle, it is possible to postpone diabetes. An obese person with a family history of diabetes is expected to be physically active and to eat a balanced diet.","options":{"A":"However, people come up with all kinds of excuses when told to be physically active and to do regular exercise.","B":"Why do people find excuses for not doing exercise when they find time to sit in front of the TV for hours?","C":"The solution to this problem is to try to be physically active wherever and whenever possible.","D":"However, this seems to be the greatest challenge."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"However, this seems to be the greatest challenge.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Though it correctly uses 'however' to show contrast, it talks about only exercise — not about the diet part mentioned in the earlier sentence. Incomplete reference to both factors.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Though it correctly uses a rhetorical question, it still contains info about exercise only — not about the diet part mentioned in the earlier sentence.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Same problem as Option B — focuses only on physical activity, ignoring the dietary component mentioned in the earlier sentence.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Comprehensively refers to both factors described in the earlier sentence — 'this' refers to both being physically active AND eating a balanced diet, making it the most complete conclusion."}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"wrong_focus","C":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"When we go through the sentences, we understand that the paragraph talks about increasing incidence of diabetes and the reasons for that incidence; genetic factors and obesity because of bad lifestyle. The paragraph should continue with further information about the reasons mentioned, or perhaps the reason for the consistent increase in the number of diabetics.\\nOption A: incorrect because, though it correctly uses however to show the contrast between the following and preceding ideas, it talks about just exercise, not about the two reasons mentioned in the earlier sentence.\\nOption B: incorrect because, though it correctly uses a rhetorical question in this regard, the option still contains info about exercise, not about the diet part mentioned in the earlier sentence.\\nOption C: incorrect because of the same reason given for Option B.\\nOption D: correct because this option comprehensively refers to the factors described in the earlier sentence.\\nThus, the best option is Option D. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_018","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"The most seductive illusion of the planet we inhabit is that it is standing still. Wind blows, but trees only bend. At the river bank only the water recedes.","options":{"A":"But the reality is that the galaxy is churning.","B":"But the reality is that the solar system is turning.","C":"But the reality is that the earth is spinning around the sun.","D":"But the reality is that most creatures on earth are in constant movement."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"But the reality is that the earth is spinning around the sun.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about the galaxy, not the planet we inhabit — too broad and outside the scope of the paragraph which is specifically about Earth.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about the solar system, not specifically about the planet — still too broad.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":true,"reason":"Correctly adds the notion about the earth's movement — directly contradicts the illusion that the planet is standing still, which is the exact point of the paragraph."},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about creatures on earth, not the planet itself — the paragraph's illusion is about the planet being still, not about creature movement.","error_type":"wrong_focus"}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"wrong_focus","D":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The passage states that the illusion is that our planet is still. Thus, overall, the paragraph should end with a statement with a sense that the planet is not still or is moving.\\nOption A: incorrect because this sentence talks about galaxy, not our planet.\\nOption B: incorrect because this sentence talks about the solar system.\\nOption C: correct because it adds to the paragraph the correct notion about the earth's movement.\\nOption D: incorrect because this sentence talks about the creatures, not the planet as is required by the context.\\nThus, the correct option is Option C. Choice (C)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_019","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"What does corruption look like? The short answer is: not what you think it does. Imagine a politician being bribed. You might envisage a suitcase stuffed with used dollar bills being handed over in a dark alleyway.","options":{"A":"But nowadays, the identities of the corrupt are hidden.","B":"But nowadays, corruption does not exist.","C":"But nowadays, corruption can work differently.","D":"But nowadays, bribes go into the bank accounts of the corrupt."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"But nowadays, corruption can work differently.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about identification of the corrupt — but the paragraph talks about the forms/appearance of corruption, not about identifying who is corrupt.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"States corruption does not exist — directly contradicts the premise of the paragraph which is asking what corruption looks like.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"C":{"fits":true,"reason":"Implies the other forms in which corruption exists — 'differently' from the suitcase of cash cliché. Correctly opens the possibility of multiple forms."},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about only one additional form of corruption (bank accounts) while the paragraph hints at many forms — too specific and incomplete.","error_type":"wrong_focus"}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"contradicts_paragraph","D":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"By posing a question about corruption, the passage introduces the idea of the real form of corruption. It goes on to say that physical money may not be the only way in which corruption has its existence. Thus, naturally, the concluding sentence needs to bring out the other forms in which corruption exists.\\nOption A: incorrect because this sentence talks about the identification of corruption, while the paragraph talks about the forms of corruption.\\nOption B: incorrect because this sentence talks about the non-existence of corruption, while the given paragraph does not imply this.\\nOption C: correct because this implies the other forms of corruption.\\nOption D: incorrect because it talks about only one additional form of corruption, while the paragraph hints at many forms of corruption.\\nThus, the best option is Option C. Choice (C)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_020","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"last_sentence","paragraph":"And this is not the first time the man has shot his mouth off. Earlier, when a journalist asked him why women in his State were malnourished, he aimed another salvo that bordered on idiocy, expounding on how girls were beauty-conscious and not health-conscious and, hence resorted to dieting by refusing to drink milk. What he forgot to add was the very same girls had no food to eat in the first place!","options":{"A":"This is much akin to the saying, 'The worst wheel of a cart makes the most noise.'","B":"This is much akin to what somebody said, 'I am invincible! Hence, I can talk rubbish and get away with impunity!'","C":"This illustrates the statement somebody made, 'The difference is that a statesman thinks he belongs to the State, and a politician thinks the State belongs to him.'","D":"This is much akin to Marie Antoinette's, 'Let them eat cake!' retort."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"This is much akin to Marie Antoinette's, 'Let them eat cake!' retort.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"The 'worst wheel making most noise' is about noisy complaints, not about callous dismissal of poverty — does not bring out the meaning implicit in the context.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"About invincibility and impunity — not relevant to the callous dismissal of malnourishment.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"About the difference between statesmen and politicians — not related to the specific callousness about food deprivation.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"The penultimate sentence gives the clue — 'the same girls had no food to eat in the first place'. This context directly parallels Marie Antoinette's famous retort about eating cake when there is no bread."}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"out_of_scope","C":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The penultimate sentence of the paragraph gives the clue – 'the same girls had no food to eat in the first place'. This context reminds us of Marie Antoinette's famous retort that they could eat cake if they had no bread.\\nOption A: This option does not bring out the meaning implicit in the context\\nOption B: This option is also not relevant to the context.\\nOption C: This option is not related to what the paragraph intends to convey.\\nOption D: Correct. This option is correct based on the explanation given at the beginning.\\nThus, the best option is Option D. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 1 to 20: The following questions have a paragraph from which the last sentence has been deleted. From the given options, choose the one that completes the paragraph in the most appropriate way."},{"id":"PC_E5_021","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"Scientists are increasingly investigating the role circadian rhythms play in the development of diabetes. (______). Some of the health concerns are, sleep-wake cycles, circadian rhythms also regulate hormones that affect metabolism, appetite, insulin, and blood glucose. When circadian rhythms are out of sync, the body's metabolic health can decline and a risk for diabetes can increase.","options":{"A":"Circadian rhythms affect many areas of your health, some of which you might not be aware of.","B":"Despite the increasingly strong evidence linking sleep to diabetes, sleep problems remain an overlooked factor in the risk for and management of the disease.","C":"Poor sleep interferes with insulin and blood glucose thereby leading to diabetes.","D":"Sleep disruption increases the risk of Type II diabetes."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Circadian rhythms affect many areas of your health, some of which you might not be aware of.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"Forms an appropriate link between the first sentence (scientists investigating circadian rhythms and diabetes) and the last two sentences (listing the various metabolic functions affected) — lays emphasis on the broad importance of circadian rhythms."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Mentions 'the disease' vaguely and does not form a logical link between the statements — also the focus on sleep problems being overlooked doesn't bridge to the metabolic list that follows.","error_type":"vague"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Already stated in the paragraph — the following sentences explicitly mention insulin and blood glucose.","error_type":"redundant"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"A repetition of what is already stated in the paragraph.","error_type":"redundant"}},"common_errors":{"B":"vague","C":"redundant","D":"redundant"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The first sentence states that scientists are investigating the role circadian rhythm plays in the development of diabetes. The sentence which follows the blank lists out the various metabolic functions which get affected if the circadian gets disrupted. The sentence which links these two sentences should lay emphasis on the importance of circadian rhythms in regulating bodily functions. Only option A forms an appropriate link between the first sentence and the last two sentences of the paragraph.\\nChoice A: CORRECT due to the explanation given above.\\nChoice B: This statement which tells that sleep problems remain an overlooked factor in the management of \\"the disease\\" is rather vague and does not form a logical link between the statements.\\nChoice C: This is already stated in the paragraph.\\nChoice D: This is a repetition of what is already stated in the paragraph. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_022","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"India was the first country to attain independence after World War II. The Indian anti-colonial struggle left a deep impact on the political developments of other Asian and African countries. (______)","options":{"A":"Africans used the methods successfully tried by India in their struggle for freedom.","B":"India extended a hand of friendship and cooperation to Africans in their struggle against colonialism and racialism.","C":"Even Asian countries like Japan and Indonesia were colonized by the British.","D":"Many other colonies drew inspiration from India."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Africans used the methods successfully tried by India in their struggle for freedom.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"Correctly explains that Africans emulated the Indians in their struggle for freedom — a specific elaboration of the 'deep impact' mentioned in the preceding sentence."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about India extending friendship and cooperation — this does not explain the deep impact that India's anti-colonial struggle left on other countries.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The paragraph is about India's influence on other colonies — introducing Japan and Indonesia being colonised by the British is irrelevant to the impact of India's struggle.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Too vague — 'many other colonies' is not specific enough to the discussion about other Asian and African colonies mentioned in the preceding sentence.","error_type":"vague"}},"common_errors":{"B":"wrong_focus","C":"out_of_scope","D":"vague"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"Indian freedom struggle was a role model for other colonial countries. Thus, the Africans emulated the Indians in their struggle for freedom. Choice A explains this appropriately.\\nChoice A : CORRECT according to the explanation given above.\\nChoice B : This option does not explain the deep impact which India's anti-colonial struggle left on other Asian and African countries.\\nChoice C : This option can also be eliminated based on the explanation given for the previous option.\\nChoice D : The sentence that precedes the blank talks about the impact which India's anti-colonial struggle left on other Asian and African countries. Therefore, this option which talks about other colonies is rather vague and not relevant to the discussion about other Asian and African colonies. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_023","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"(______) There are several cave paintings, stone engravings and carved figures which bear this out. The Neanderthal man attempted this too, but his drawings of the tools he used show that they were rather crude.","options":{"A":"Prehistoric man used sophisticated tools for drawing and carving figures.","B":"The Cro-Magnon man, who was the forerunner of modern man, earned his daily bread through paintings.","C":"The Cro-Magnon man, who was the forerunner of modern man, was the first fine artist in the history of man's evolution.","D":"Prehistoric man pursued painting and carving figures as a hobby."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Prehistoric man used sophisticated tools for drawing and carving figures.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"Contrasts the sophisticated tools used by prehistoric man with the crude ones used by Neanderthal man — the most logical opening statement that the subsequent sentences bear out."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"The paragraph does not mention anything about how prehistoric man earned his daily bread — out of scope.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not mention anything about the tools used — not in sync with the last sentence which specifically compares tools between Cro-Magnon and Neanderthal man.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Inappropriate compared to Option A — does not mention tools which is the key focus of the last sentence.","error_type":"wrong_focus"}},"common_errors":{"B":"out_of_scope","C":"wrong_focus","D":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The second line states, \\"There were……. Figures which bear this out. He attempted to create his daily life through this. The Neanderthal man attempted this too, but his drawings of the tools…….. So, we need a statement in the blank which is a general statement on the pre-historic man and drawing/painting.\\nChoice A : CORRECT. This option which contrasts the sophisticated tools used by pre historic man with the crude ones used by Neanderthal man is most logical as the opening statement.\\nChoice B : The paragraph does not mention anything about how pre-historic man earned his daily bread.\\nChoice C : Although this option seems to be a probable answer, this option can be eliminated because it does not mention anything about the tools used and is, therefore, not in sync with the last sentence of the passage which talks about the tools used by the Neanderthal man.\\nChoice D : Even this option seems close but is inappropriate compared to option A and can be eliminated based on the explanation given for option C. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_024","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"The natural atmosphere which man has inherited from the past, has been deteriorating under the impact of industrialization. Factories pump millions of tons of dust into the air, vehicles spread fumes and sprays are used to kill agricultural pests – all combine to change the ideal picture. (______) The situation near big cities and heavily industrialized areas has become particularly bad, and the air is not fit for breathing.","options":{"A":"Movement of vehicular traffic on the roads should be restricted.","B":"The pollution of air has become a matter of great concern because it continues to increase as civilization spreads.","C":"Society will have to move towards stricter pollution control.","D":"The atmosphere should be protected as it is a great and irreplaceable resource for living."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"The pollution of air has become a matter of great concern because it continues to increase as civilization spreads.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"This solution statement could follow the last sentence but cannot precede it — it suggests a solution before the full problem is established.","error_type":"wrong_stage"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"Explains how air pollution has increased with the spread of civilization — bridges the second sentence (causes of pollution) with the last sentence (severity near cities)."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"A solution statement that could follow the last sentence but cannot logically precede it.","error_type":"wrong_stage"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Generic tone — cannot form a logical link with the remaining statements of the paragraph.","error_type":"vague"}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_stage","C":"wrong_stage","D":"vague"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The first sentence talks about the deterioration of the earth's natural atmosphere due to air pollution. The second sentence elaborates on the cause for pollution Sentence B explains how air pollution has increased with the spread of civilization. This sentence explains the last sentence of the paragraph.\\nChoice A : This statement which suggests a solution to the problem can follow the last statement.\\nChoice B : CORRECT according to the explanation given above.\\nChoice C : This option can also follow the last statement but cannot precede the it.\\nChoice D : This option has a generic tone and cannot form a logical link with the remaining statements of the paragraph. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_025","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"For several thousands of years, the moon has been the only satellite of the earth. Today, however, the earth has many other satellites – all made by man. (______) However, some of them will still be going around the earth thousands of years from now.","options":{"A":"Artificial satellites do not fall because they are not affected by earth's gravity.","B":"They travel in an orbit around the earth.","C":"As they speed along, they tend to go straight off into space.","D":"These artificial satellites are very much smaller than the moon."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"These artificial satellites are very much smaller than the moon.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not explain the contrast indicated in the last sentence — the contrast is about size and longevity, not about gravity.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"The orbit information does not form a logical link with the last sentence about satellites continuing for thousands of years.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Focuses on the speed of satellites but does not form a logical link with the last statement about continuing to go around the earth for thousands of years.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Despite being smaller than the moon, artificial satellites will still revolve around the earth even after several years — the contrast between smallness and longevity bridges the second and last sentences."}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"wrong_focus","C":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Choice D speaks about artificial satellites, which though smaller than the moon will revolve around the earth even after several years. The sentence emphasizes the power of artificial satellites.\\nChoice A : This option does not explain the contrast indicated in the last sentence of the paragraph.\\nChoice B : This option can also be eliminated based on the explanation given for the previous option.\\nChoice C : This option focusses on the speed of the satellites and does not form a logical link with the last statement of the paragraph.\\nChoice D : CORRECT based on the explanation given in the previous statement. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_026","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"It would always be a good idea to do good things that bring happiness to others. If an individual is not able to bring happiness to others, it is certainly a good idea to refrain from causing unhappiness to others. (______) It reminds man of the nature of his relationship with the universe, more so, since it is the day on which the earth begins a new revolution around the sun.","options":{"A":"People feel that it is a good idea to make resolutions to alter their ways of living on the beginning of the year.","B":"Ultimately, the responsibility for one's destiny rests totally with the individual himself.","C":"Since man tends to either be ignorant or forget this principle, New Year is an important time for making a fresh start and resolutions for the future.","D":"New Year's Day is a time to remind people of the eternal movement that is the law and pulse of the universe."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"Since man tends to either be ignorant or forget this principle, New Year is an important time for making a fresh start and resolutions for the future.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not form a logical link either with the statement preceding the blank or the statement following it.","error_type":"disrupts_logical_flow"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Rather ambiguous and cannot be linked to any of the given statements in context.","error_type":"vague"},"C":{"fits":true,"reason":"'This principle' refers to the principle of bringing happiness or refraining from causing unhappiness; 'it' in the following sentence refers to New Year in statement C — a perfect bridge."},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Cannot form a logical link with the second sentence — 'It reminds man' in the following sentence requires 'New Year' as the antecedent, which C provides but D does not set up.","error_type":"disrupts_logical_flow"}},"common_errors":{"A":"disrupts_logical_flow","B":"vague","D":"disrupts_logical_flow"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Sentence C speaks about the importance of New Year's Day for making resolutions and is thus linked to the sentence which follows the blank. 'This principle' in C refers to the principle mentioned in the first sentence and the pronoun 'it' refers to New Year in statement C.\\nChoice A : This statement does not form a logical link either with the statement preceding the blank or that which follows it.\\nChoice B : This statement is rather ambiguous and cannot be linked to any of the given statements.\\nChoice C : CORRECT according to the explanation given at the beginning.\\nChoice D : This statement cannot form a logical link with the second statement. Choice (C)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_027","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"Most of us form opinions about people, events, circumstances and situations. Our opinions depend predominantly on our own character, behaviour and prevailing circumstances. (______)","options":{"A":"Most of us in society depend and act based on others' opinions of us.","B":"Hence, when there are changes in these factors, our opinions also change.","C":"We should develop a very good personality to boost the positiveness in our opinion about self.","D":"Hence, it is important for all of us not to depend on others' opinions."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Hence, when there are changes in these factors, our opinions also change.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"States that our actions are based on others' opinions of us — not in sync with the preceding statements which talk about how we form opinions about others.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"Explains what forms the basis for forming and changing opinions — 'these factors' refers to character, behaviour and prevailing circumstances in the preceding sentence."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Advisory tone about developing a good personality — does not gel with the previous statements which describe how opinions are formed, not what we should do.","error_type":"tone_mismatch"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Advisory tone — not connected with the two preceding statements which talk about how we form opinions about others, not about depending on others' opinions of us.","error_type":"tone_mismatch"}},"common_errors":{"A":"contradicts_paragraph","C":"tone_mismatch","D":"tone_mismatch"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"Choice B explains what forms the basis for forming and changing opinions.\\nChoice A : This option, which states that our actions are based on others' opinions of us, is not in sync with the preceding statements which talk about how we form opinions about others.\\nChoice B : CORRECT according to the explanations given above.\\nChoice C : This statement, which says what we should do to boost positiveness in our opinion about ourselves, does not gel with the previous statements.\\nChoice D : even this option has an advisory tone and is not connected with the two preceding statements which talk about how we form opinions about others. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_028","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"Convergence of technologies primarily calls for a networked environment. In such an environment, network engineers are required to keep the system up and running all the time. (______) At the entry level, technical skills are considered more important than conceptual skills which accrue through experience.","options":{"A":"Networking is a high priority area in the corporate world.","B":"Large corporates are in the process of setting up intranets connecting all their offices and extranets linking up vendors and dealers.","C":"They need to be well-versed in communication skills.","D":"They need to have well-honed technical skills."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"They need to have well-honed technical skills.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not talk about technical skills and cannot be connected to the last sentence which specifically focuses on technical skills.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not mention anything about networking engineers and the need for technical skills — doesn't form a sequence with the surrounding sentences.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"The focus in the surrounding sentences is on technical skills, not communication skills — the wrong type of skill.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Speaks about the technical skills required by network engineers — bridges the demand for network engineers and the last sentence's statement about technical skills being most important at entry level."}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"wrong_focus","C":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The sentence preceding the blank talks about the demand for network engineers to manage the networked environment facilitated by the convergence of technologies. The sentence that follows the blank talks about the need for technical skills at the entry level. Choice D which speaks about the technical skills required by a network engineer explains the preceding and subsequent sentences.\\nChoice A : This statement does not talk about technical skills and cannot, therefore, be connected to the last sentence of the paragraph.\\nChoice B : This option also does not mention anything about networking engineers and the need for technical skills and does not form a sequence with the sentences preceding and following it.\\nChoice C : The focus, in the sentences preceding and following the blank are on technical skills and not on communication skills.\\nChoice D : CORRECT according to the explanation given at the beginning. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_029","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"Environmental degradation is a matter of great concern to us. (______) We must distinguish between environmental decay as it continues to take place on its own and the one caused by man. It should be realised that some decay is natural and unavoidable and there simply is nothing that we can do about it.","options":{"A":"We have no option, but to take it as a fact of life.","B":"If our race did not exist at all, the global ecosystem would continue to decay, inspite of us.","C":"It should however be remembered that all environmental degradation is not man made.","D":"The difference between environmental decay and environmental pollution is easy to see."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"It should however be remembered that all environmental degradation is not man made.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Not connected to the sentence that follows — 'take it as a fact of life' doesn't lead to distinguishing between natural and man-made decay.","error_type":"disrupts_logical_flow"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Not connected to the sentence that follows — the counterfactual about our race not existing doesn't bridge to the distinction that follows.","error_type":"disrupts_logical_flow"},"C":{"fits":true,"reason":"Explains that man is not totally responsible for environmental degradation — directly leads to the next sentence about distinguishing natural decay from man-made decay."},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Brings in a comparison between environmental decay and environmental pollution that is not warranted in the given context.","error_type":"out_of_scope"}},"common_errors":{"A":"disrupts_logical_flow","B":"disrupts_logical_flow","D":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The sentence that follows the blank talks about distinguishing between environmental decay that is caused on its own and that which is caused by man. Choice C explains that man is not totally responsible for environmental degradation, thus it explains the following sentence.\\nChoice A : This is not connected to the sentence that follows the blank.\\nChoice B : This statement is also not connected to the sentence that follows the blank.\\nChoice C : CORRECT based on the explanation given above.\\nChoice D : This option brings in a comparison that is not warranted in the given context. Choice (C)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_030","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"In African areas where colonialism introduced European settlement, the societies were structured on the basis of racial discrimination. (______) Africans were denied the right to vote or lease their land. They were forced to work on low wages.","options":{"A":"Racial discrimination tried to reduce the African to subhuman levels.","B":"In the past discrimination was based on religion, region or caste.","C":"There is no proper existence of the societies.","D":"Till the 16th century, inferiority was not associated with Asians or Africans."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"Racial discrimination tried to reduce the African to subhuman levels.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"Explains that racial discrimination reduced Africans to very low levels — directly supported by the subsequent sentences about denial of voting rights and forced low-wage labour."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"What factors were responsible for discrimination in the past is not relevant to the discussion about colonial racial discrimination in Africa.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Rather vague and cannot be connected either to the sentence preceding or following the blank.","error_type":"vague"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"The paragraph is specific to racial discrimination in Africa — introducing inferiority not being associated with Asians before the 16th century is not pertinent.","error_type":"out_of_scope"}},"common_errors":{"B":"out_of_scope","C":"vague","D":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"Choice A : CORRECT explains that racial discrimination in Africa reduced people to very low levels which is supported by the subsequent sentences.\\nChoice B : What are the factors which are responsible for leading to discrimination is not relevant to the discussion at hand.\\nChoice C : This option is rather vague and cannot be connected either to the sentence preceding the blank or the sentence that follow it.\\nChoice D : The paragraph is specific to racial discrimination in Africa, therefore this option is not pertinent to the discussion at hand. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_031","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"One major change in careers is that one can work from home. (______) So far, only work relating to Information Technology has been thus affected. It is expected that many other careers will afford this flexibility in the future.","options":{"A":"Therefore, one should develop a confident, outgoing personality.","B":"There is no such thing as a permanent job.","C":"New technologies ensure that geographical distance is not a hindrance to one's work.","D":"While it is true that people will switch jobs faster than ever before, one must be loyal to one's organisation."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"New technologies ensure that geographical distance is not a hindrance to one's work.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Completely unrelated to the topic of working from home and geographical flexibility.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not form a logical connection with the first sentence about working from home or the following sentences about IT work.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":true,"reason":"Supports the first sentence (working from home is possible) and explains the following sentences (IT work is currently affected, others will be in the future) — technology removes the hindrance of geographical distance."},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not explain the topic of working from home discussed in the preceding and following statements.","error_type":"out_of_scope"}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","B":"out_of_scope","D":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"Sentence C is the ideal choice because it supports the previous sentence and explains the subsequent sentences.\\nChoice A : This option is completely unrelated to the topic at hand.\\nChoice B : This option does not form a logical connection either with the first sentence or with the subsequent sentences.\\nChoice C : CORRECT according to the explanation given above.\\nChoice D : This option does not explain the topic of working from home discussed in the preceding statements. Choice (C)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_032","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"Population growth and economic development leading to rising standards of living of a country act and react on each other. In our country, particularly in urban areas, better off families are smaller in size than the poorer families. (______)","options":{"A":"A rise in population marks a growth in productivity.","B":"Developed Western countries are able to cope with the tension between population growth and standards of livings.","C":"Rapid increase in population may have an adverse impact on the pace of economic development.","D":"If development is not fast enough to meet the needs of the population, poverty and over population will result."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"If development is not fast enough to meet the needs of the population, poverty and over population will result.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Runs contrary to what is stated in the paragraph — a rise in population does not mark growth in productivity in the context described.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Rather digressing — not relevant to the discussion about population-development interaction in the Indian context.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"A restatement of the same idea discussed in the preceding sentences — adds nothing new.","error_type":"redundant"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"The first sentence talks about population growth and economic development as interacting; the second sentence speaks about population, so the subsequent should logically speak about development consequences — Option D does this."}},"common_errors":{"A":"contradicts_paragraph","B":"out_of_scope","C":"redundant"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The first sentence talks about how population growth economic development are related. The second sentence speaks about population growth so the subsequent should logically speak about development. Hence choice D is appropriate.\\nChoice A : This option runs contrary to what is stated in the paragraph.\\nChoice B : This option is rather digressing and is not relevant to the discussion at hand.\\nChoice C : This sentence is a restatement of the same idea discussed in the preceding sentences.\\nChoice D : CORRECT according to the explanation given at the beginning. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_033","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"Traditionally, the scourge of pestilence and epidemics led to a massive scale of mortality of human population and of cattle in villages. Small pox, cholera and plague instilled mystical terror in the hearts of the people. (______) It contributed to erroneous religious beliefs.","options":{"A":"The cases of possession were too frequent both for men and women in villages.","B":"This terror was often beyond human control and hence bred fatalism, superstition and ritualistic obscurantism.","C":"This has inspired confidence among people.","D":"All this has severely eroded people's faith in superstitious beliefs."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"This terror was often beyond human control and hence bred fatalism, superstition and ritualistic obscurantism.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not discuss 'the terror' discussed in the previous statement — introduces possession without connection to the mystical terror.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"'This' refers to the 'mystical terror' in the preceding sentence — explains how the terror bred fatalism and superstition, leading directly to the erroneous religious beliefs in the following sentence."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Mystical terror cannot inspire confidence in people — directly contradicts the context.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not gel with the last sentence — erroneous religious beliefs cannot lead to eroding faith in superstitious beliefs; the direction is reversed.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","C":"contradicts_paragraph","D":"contradicts_paragraph"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The sentence preceding the blank talks about how certain epidemics instilled mystical terror in the hearts of people. \\"This\\" in option B refers to the \\"mystical terror\\" mentioned in the previous statement. Choice B explains the misconception pertaining to diseases in the olden days, thereby leading to erroneous religious beliefs.\\nChoice A : This option does not discuss \\"the terror\\" discussed in the previous statement.\\nChoice B : CORRECT according to the explanation given at the beginning.\\nChoice C : This option is rather absurd because \\"mystical terror\\" cannot inspire confidence in people.\\nChoice D : This option does not gel with the last sentence of the paragraph because erroneous religious beliefs cannot lead to confidence among people. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_034","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"One of the most glaring and visible sights in the urban areas is proliferation of women workers. (______) The proliferation of administrative jobs both in public and private sector created a demand for educated personnel. Developmental activities and welfare work also created openings for scientific, technical, medical and para-medical persons.","options":{"A":"The rising cost of living, access to education and social changes in urban areas have led to the withdrawal of the taboos that earlier affected women of higher classes.","B":"Society still considers women as home makers.","C":"An out-side job, however prestigious or lucrative it is, does not absolve women from their familial role.","D":"Women have to live within the male dominated family structure."},"correct_answer":"A","correct_answer_value":"The rising cost of living, access to education and social changes in urban areas have led to the withdrawal of the taboos that earlier affected women of higher classes.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":true,"reason":"Explains the circumstances that led to the proliferation of women workers — bridges the first sentence (proliferation) with the following sentences (types of jobs that created demand for women)."},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Carries information not pertinent to the point discussed — the paragraph is about why women entered the workforce, not about societal perceptions.","error_type":"tone_mismatch"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Not pertinent to the topic of discussion — about familial role, not about the reasons for workforce proliferation.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not form a logical link either with the sentence preceding or following the blank.","error_type":"out_of_scope"}},"common_errors":{"B":"tone_mismatch","C":"out_of_scope","D":"out_of_scope"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The first sentence talks about the proliferation of women workers. The sentences following the blank talk about the various kinds of jobs which led to the proliferation of women workers. The sentence which links the first sentence with the subsequent sentences should explain the circumstances which led to the proliferation of women workers. Only choice A satisfies this condition.\\nChoice A : CORRECT according to the explanation given above.\\nChoice B : This information carries information which is not pertinent to the point discussed in the paragraph.\\nChoice C : This option is also not pertinent to the topic of discussion.\\nChoice D : This option does not form a logical link either with the sentence preceding the blank or those that follow the blank. Choice (A)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_035","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"Science is the means by which the whole of our civilisation is rapidly being transformed. (______) But now science is progressing by leaps and bounds, for all to see. The fabric of our civilisation has changed enormously in our own lifetime and is changing more and more rapidly from year to year.","options":{"A":"Ancient society was not congenial for the development of science.","B":"In order to understand the present and to control the future, it is necessary to know the history of science.","C":"In the past, science grew steadily and imperceptibly.","D":"In order to draw full benefits from science, we have to understand how science is related to social and economic factors."},"correct_answer":"C","correct_answer_value":"In the past, science grew steadily and imperceptibly.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"The sentence fitting the blank should talk about the growth of science in the past to contrast with 'leaps and bounds' — Option A talks about society's congenitality, not science's rate of growth.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about understanding the history of science — not related to the topic of the rate of science's growth.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"C":{"fits":true,"reason":"The sentence following the blank uses 'but now' to contrast with steady past growth — Option C correctly provides the past state (steady and imperceptible) that 'but now' contrasts with."},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Could follow the last sentence but cannot form a logical link with the sentence preceding the blank or that following it.","error_type":"wrong_stage"}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"out_of_scope","D":"wrong_stage"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The first sentence states that science is rapidly transforming our society and the sentence following the blank explains that science is now progressing by leaps and bounds. The sentence bridging these two sentences should present a contrast with the second sentence which presents a contrasting idea using the conjunction \\"but\\". Choice C, which explains the difference in the growth rate of science in the past and present years is ideal to fit into the blank.\\nChoice A : The sentence which fits into the blank should talk about the growth of science in the past thereby forming a logical link with the sentence that follows the blank.\\nChoice B : This option talks, which talks about the need to know the history of science, is not related to the topic of discussion.\\nChoice C : CORRECT based on the explanation given at the beginning.\\nChoice D : This statement can follow the last sentence but it cannot form a logical link either with the sentence preceding the blank or that which follows it. Choice (C)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_036","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"(______) To begin with they must have collected anything they could eat – seeds, nuts, fruits, roots, honey and any small animal that could be caught with bare hands. The largest food sharing unit tended to concentrate upon a certain type of food which was easily available to them in plenty. Thus, human groups eating one type of food came to consider themselves as 'Kins' or fellow beings of the same community or clan.","options":{"A":"Earliest human groups entirely depended on hunting animals for their food.","B":"The social life of the earliest human groups of tribes revolved around food gathering.","C":"Food gathering was the only preoccupation in the life of the early man.","D":"Early man's survival depended entirely on nature."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"The social life of the earliest human groups of tribes revolved around food gathering.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about hunting animals for food — cannot be linked to the paragraph which talks about food gathering (seeds, nuts, fruits, roots), not hunting.","error_type":"contradicts_paragraph"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"Forms the opening sentence by explaining how ancient man's life revolved around food gathering — forming a logical link with the subsequent sentences about gathering, sharing food and development of kinship."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Inappropriate compared to Option B — does not mention anything about the social life of ancient man which is what the paragraph elaborates on.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Not logical in the given context — too vague and doesn't connect to food gathering or social life.","error_type":"vague"}},"common_errors":{"A":"contradicts_paragraph","C":"wrong_focus","D":"vague"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"Choice B forms the opening sentence of the paragraph, by explaining how the ancient man's life revolved around food gathering and thereby forming a logical link with the subsequent sentences of the paragraph which explain how gathering and sharing of food and the development of kinship.\\nChoice A : This option which talks about hunting animals for food cannot be linked to the given paragraph which talks about food gathering.\\nChoice B : CORRECT according to the explanation given above.\\nChoice C : This option is inappropriate when compared to option B as it does not mention anything about the social life of ancient man.\\nChoice D : This option is also not logical in the given context. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_037","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"We have already exhausted the traditional sources. (______) If we achieve in this area there will be no cause for frustration.","options":{"A":"Now we have to reduce the number of industries.","B":"Now we have to go in search of non-conventional sources of energy.","C":"Now we have to bargain with foreign countries.","D":"Now we have to find out a substitute for power."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Now we have to go in search of non-conventional sources of energy.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"'Industries' are not related to 'traditional sources' mentioned in the first statement — the context is about energy sources, not industries.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"The logic flows: we have exhausted traditional sources → so we must search for non-conventional energy sources → if we achieve this, no frustration. 'Non-conventional sources' directly contrasts with 'traditional sources'."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Bargaining with foreign countries is ambiguous and doesn't connect the exhaustion of traditional sources with the achievement goal.","error_type":"vague"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Finding a substitute for power is less specific than non-conventional energy sources — Option B more precisely contrasts with 'traditional sources'.","error_type":"vague"}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","C":"vague","D":"vague"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The logic can be started thus: We have exhausted traditional sources. So, we must search for non-conventional energy sources. There will be no frustration if we succeed in this endeavour.\\nChoice A : \\"Industries\\" are not related to the \\"traditional sources\\" mentioned in the first statement\\nChoice B : CORRECT based on the explanation given above.\\nChoice C : Even this statement becomes rather ambiguous when placed between the two given sentences.\\nChoice D : This statement is inappropriate compared to option B because \\"non-conventional sources of energy\\" in B presents a contrast with the \\"traditional sources\\" mentioned in the first statement. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_038","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"Students are full of energy and enthusiasm. They have a natural predilection for justice and for fair play. (______) Students have spearheaded many national movements and have brought about radical changes.","options":{"A":"They have enough time to do whatever they like.","B":"They have no responsibility and have nothing to loose.","C":"No one will question their right to fight.","D":"Their young minds can purify the politics of our country of all dross and stench."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Their young minds can purify the politics of our country of all dross and stench.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Cannot be linked to 'predilection for justice and fair play' in the preceding sentence — having free time doesn't connect to justice.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"Has a rather negative tone — cannot form a logical link with the last sentence about spearheading national movements which has a positive sense.","error_type":"tone_mismatch"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Cannot form a logical link with either the preceding statement about justice/fair play or the following statement about national movements.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"Predilection for justice makes it possible for students to purify politics — directly bridges the justice/fair play trait with the national movement achievements."}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","B":"tone_mismatch","C":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"Predilection for justice makes it possible for the students to purify our politics. Hence choice D is the most logical in the given context.\\nChoice A : This option cannot be linked to \\"predilection and fair play mentioned in the sentence preceding the blank.\\nChoice B : This option has a rather negative tone and cannot form a logical link with the last sentence – spearheaded many national movements – which has a positive sense.\\nChoice C : Even this option cannot form a logical link either with the statement which precedes the blank or the last statement.\\nChoice D : CORRECT based on the explanation given above. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_039","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"A great leader has something timeless about him and he remains consequential. He cannot be deprived of the credit for the services he rendered and the values he stood for, even if his ideas and policies become passé and even if the rulers of the day find his memory inconvenient or unprofitable. (______). Jawaharlal Nehru is one such leader that modern India produced.","options":{"A":"Over and above any virtue, there is the matter of temperament that gives a leader his character.","B":"Above all, people's collective memory will not allow him to fade into oblivion.","C":"A less competent leader would be driven either by the mob or become a dictator.","D":"The commitment to the institutions of state is one of the most important virtues of a leader."},"correct_answer":"B","correct_answer_value":"Above all, people's collective memory will not allow him to fade into oblivion.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about one of the virtues of a leader — not about the abiding nature of his persona which the paragraph argues will not be forgotten.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"B":{"fits":true,"reason":"Conforms to the idea of something timeless about a great leader — people's collective memory ensures he cannot be forgotten, directly connecting to both the preceding sentences and the Nehru example."},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Has a negative connotation and is a misfit — the paragraph is about great leaders, not about less competent ones.","error_type":"tone_mismatch"},"D":{"fits":false,"reason":"Talks about one of the general virtues of a leader — not about the abiding, timeless quality of a great leader.","error_type":"wrong_focus"}},"common_errors":{"A":"wrong_focus","C":"tone_mismatch","D":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"medium","explanation":"The paragraph states that there is something eternal about a good leader. The services that he rendered and the values he stood for continue to be abiding even if his ideas and policies become passé with the passage of time. The penultimate sentence should convey the same sense given by the first two sentences and should logically connect the first sentence with the last sentence of the paragraph which states that Jawaharlal Nehru embodied all these qualities.\\nChoice A: This statement cannot form a logically coherent paragraph because it talks about one of the virtues of a leader and not about the abiding nature of his persona which will not be forgotten even with the passage of time.\\nChoice B: CORRECT. This statement conforms to the explanation given above and forms a logically coherent paragraph along with the remaining sentences.\\nChoice C: This statement, which has a negative connotation, is a misfit in the given context.\\nChoice D: This statement also talks about one of the general virtues of a leader and not about his abiding qualities. Choice (B)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."},{"id":"PC_E5_040","exercise":"exercise_5","type":"para_completion","subtype":"middle_sentence","paragraph":"An Engineer has a sense of satisfaction that he is actively helping in the advancement of his country. (______) Big dams, buildings, bridges, etc. inspire a sense of awe.","options":{"A":"He has enough opportunity to amass money.","B":"No one else has such great opportunities to satisfy personal desires.","C":"His work is easy and it involves no danger.","D":"Further, engineering work itself is very interesting."},"correct_answer":"D","correct_answer_value":"Further, engineering work itself is very interesting.","option_analysis":{"A":{"fits":false,"reason":"Cannot be related to 'advancement of one's country' — amassing money is a personal motive, not connected to national advancement or the sense of awe.","error_type":"out_of_scope"},"B":{"fits":false,"reason":"'Personal advancement' does not gel with 'advancement of one's country' — the paragraph is about professional and national satisfaction, not personal desires.","error_type":"tone_mismatch"},"C":{"fits":false,"reason":"Does not explain the 'sense of awe' mentioned in the last sentence — easy and danger-free work doesn't connect to the awe of big dams and bridges.","error_type":"wrong_focus"},"D":{"fits":true,"reason":"The given sentences talk of 'satisfaction' and 'awe' — 'interesting' fits with these positive feelings about engineering work. 'Further' continues from the satisfaction mentioned in the first sentence."}},"common_errors":{"A":"out_of_scope","B":"tone_mismatch","C":"wrong_focus"},"difficulty":"easy","explanation":"The given sentences talk of 'satisfaction' and 'awe'. 'interesting' fits with these. Hence choice D is the most appropriate option.\\nChoice A : This option cannot be related to \\"advancement of one's country\\".\\nChoice B : \\"Personal advancement\\" does not gel with \\"advancement of one's country\\".\\nChoice C : This option does not explain the \\"sense of awe\\" mentioned in the last sentence.\\nChoice D : CORRECT according to the explanation given above. Choice (D)","time_benchmark_seconds":90,"instructions":"Directions for questions 21 to 40: In each of the following questions, a paragraph with a 'blank' is given. From the four choices select the sentence, which can go into the blank to make the paragraph logically coherent."}]`);export{e as default};
